244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (These are interesting by the way: this means that the peer that announced the header of that block first to your node at 15:51:47.110, did so with an INV message \(instead of a compact block announcement\), but then did not give you the block body for ten minutes after your node requested it. Block processing got stalled out by the peer, and you also did not receive a high-bandwidth compact block announcement for the block.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [32]
>>
