/E (Our client will be built on Core because that's the conservative choice. We're not re-architecting the software. We're differentiating on development process, policy defaults, and priorities. What gets merged, how fast things move, and who has a seat at the table when decisions are made. The underlying consensus code stays compatible, which means node operators can switch with much less risk.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
